    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0609" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg481"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 344.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Langston</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-01-02"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 2,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 321.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge, with approval, the
                    receipt of your No. 692 of the 4th ultimo in regard to the imprisonment of Mr.
                    C. A. Van Bokkelen, at Port-au-Prince, for debt, and to say that a copy of your
                    dispatch has been transmitted to his father, Mr. W. K. Van Bokkelen, at New
                    York, in response to his letter of the 25th ultimo, a copy of which, as a matter
                    of record, I herewith inclose.</p>
                <p>You will continue to exert every proper effort in Mr. Van Bokkelen’s behalf to
                    secure his early release.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d344-a1.xml" xpointer="d344-a1"/>
